    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.28) anchoring the lineup, representing our highest-probability drivers for R, HR, and RBI production. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a premier matchup against Pecko, whose 5.95 xERA suggests a prime environment for our second baseman to exploit a +19% SP skill advantage and a favorable batting order position. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** remains a staple in the outfield, bolstered by a +9% SP skill boost against Elder; his consistency allows us to navigate a day where several other starters face high-end pitching. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.26) also provides significant utility depth, benefiting from a soft matchup against Lugo (4.55 xERA) despite a slight platoon drag.\n\nOur most critical decision was the exclusion of **Miguel Vargas** (39.59), who fell just below the threshold for activation despite a solid xwOBA of 0.389. Ultimately, the optimizer penalized **Miguel Vargas** for a brutal matchup against Jacob deGrom, whose elite profile (-19% SP skill) creates too high a floor risk for our roster goals. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Sam Antonacci** and **Jackson Merrill**, as both are currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status; if either is dropped in the order or scratched, we will lose the expected stability of their projected production. Additionally, we are monitoring the risks associated with **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill**, both of whom must contend with elite-tier opposing arms in Harrison and Skenes. With **Jordan Westburg**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jacob Wilson** sidelined on the IL, our depth is stretched, placing a premium on the performance of our active starters to maintain our standing in the scarce stolen base category.",
